---
layout: layouts/page.njk
permalink: /free-agents/
title: Free agents
eyebrow: Looking for a team
lede: No team this season, or not getting the minutes? Put yourself in the pool and let the teams who are short come to you.
description: Players without a team, or without game time, can join the VFL free-agent pool and be picked up by a team for the season.
heroArt:
  video: /assets/video/vfl-free-agents-board
  poster: /assets/img/visuals/vfl-free-agents-board-poster.webp
  still: /assets/img/visuals/vfl-free-agents-board.svg
  alt: "A tactics board: seven players in a 3-2-2, with passes going to an empty eighth place marked Free agent."
---
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose" data-reveal>
      <h2>Who it's for</h2>
      <p>
        Anyone in the industry, aged 18 or over, who wants a season of football and doesn't have a side to play for: your old
        team has folded or isn't entering, you've moved studio, or your team has so many players you'd spend
        the season on the bench. Meanwhile, some teams are always one keeper or two defenders short.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Is your studio's team already in the league?</strong> Talk to their captain first. If they
        tell you the squad is full, sign up here as a free agent.
      </p>
      <p>
        You join <strong>one</strong> team, for the <strong>whole season</strong>. If your current team is in
        the league too, the move is a <strong>loan</strong>: you play for your new team this season and you're
        shown on both teams' pages as on loan.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
        <h2>Four steps</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card-grid card-grid--4">
      <div class="card" data-reveal>
        <span class="card__num">Step 01</span>
        <h3>Sign up</h3>
        <p>Confirm your email with a one-time code, then tell us your positions, availability and how competitive you like it. Takes two minutes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" data-reveal>
        <span class="card__num">Step 02</span>
        <h3>Teams take a look</h3>
        <p>Captains in the league see your profile. When one is interested, they get your contact details and you see their team on your page.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" data-reveal>
        <span class="card__num">Step 03</span>
        <h3>Have a chat</h3>
        <p>They'll get in touch. Talk to as many teams as you like. When you've agreed, the team sends you an offer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" data-reveal>
        <span class="card__num">Step 04</span>
        <h3>Accept one</h3>
        <p>Accept the offer you want and you're on that team's squad for the season. The other offers close.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:2rem" data-reveal>
      <a class="btn" href="/portal/?join=free-agent" data-umami-event="Free agents: join clicked">Join the free-agent pool</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/portal/?view=agent" data-umami-event="Free agents: check offers clicked">Already signed up? Check your offers</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- The phases are set on the organisers' board (seasons.fa_phase). The squad size
    comes from site.json (registration.minSquadSize); the Phase 2 cap of four is
    the board's default: change it here too if the organisers change it there. -#}
{% set squadSize = site.registration.minSquadSize or 13 %}
<section class="section" id="phases">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">When teams can sign</div>
        <h2>The pool opens in phases</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose" data-reveal>
      <p>
        So the teams that need players most get first pick, signings happen in stages. The organisers
        announce when each one starts. You can sign up at any point until the pool closes, and your page
        always shows where things are.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Before it opens.</strong> Sign up and get your profile ready. Captains can look, but
          nobody can make offers yet.</li>
        <li><strong>Phase 1: teams that are short.</strong> Only teams with fewer than {{ squadSize }} players
          can sign free agents. If more players accept a team's offers than it has room for, the team can
          release someone. If that's you, you go straight back into the pool and other teams can sign you.</li>
        <li><strong>Phase 2: every team.</strong> Any team can sign up to four more free agents. If a team
          has used its four, it can't take your acceptance until Phase 3.</li>
        <li><strong>Phase 3: whoever's left.</strong> Any team can sign anyone still in the pool.</li>
        <li><strong>Closed.</strong> Signings are done for the season, and sign-up opens again before the
          next one.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Good to know</div>
        <h2>Your details</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose" data-reveal>
      <p>
        Your profile is only visible to the team captains in this season's league and the organisers. Your
        email address and phone number are shown only to teams that mark you as interested, and you can see
        which teams those are. A phone number is optional, but it's the quickest way for a captain to reach you.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can edit your profile, take a break from the pool or delete it at any time until you've joined a
        team. Everything is deleted at the end of the season. More in our <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Captains: the pool is on your team's page in the <a href="/portal/">team portal</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
